## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to design a CPU-friendly, real-time anomaly detector under label scarcity; covers preprocessing, model pick, online updates, drift, calibration, and evaluation in a streaming context.

## Key Concepts

- Online/streaming learning
- CPU-friendly models and latency budgeting
- Concept drift detection and calibration
- Imbalanced anomaly evaluation

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo-code for partial_fit usage (sketched)
const lr = new LogisticRegression({penalty:'l2', C:1e-4});
while (streaming){
  const batch = getNextBatch(1000);
  lr.partial_fit(batch.features, batch.labels, [0,1]);
}
```

